    <string name="pd_auto">Auto Bypass picked the fastest setting that opened %1$s/%2$s sites on this network.</string>
    <string name="pd_cn">The GFW also blocks IPs and probes actively; splitting is not enough for most sites. Only for sites caught by the SNI filter. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_custom">Your own hand-tuned setting.</string>
    <string name="pd_dns_only">No splitting, encrypted DNS only. Fastest; only defeats DNS blocking.</string>
    <string name="pd_in_id">Most blocking here is DNS-based; encrypted DNS plus light splitting is usually enough. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_ir">Byte-by-byte fragmentation with out-of-order sending. Not enough on its own for IP-blocked sites. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_kz">First-byte split with out-of-order sending and encrypted DNS. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_max">Single-byte fragmentation, out-of-order sending and encrypted DNS. Success over speed.</string>
    <string name="pd_mideast">SNI splitting with encrypted DNS; a starting point against SNI filters. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_ru">TLS record splitting with out-of-order sending and encrypted DNS. Not verified in this region: test it with Auto Bypass.</string>
    <string name="pd_ru_fake">Sends low-TTL fake ClientHello packets. Needs administrator rights. Not verified in this region.</string>
    <string name="pd_tr">Splits the ClientHello into TLS records at the SNI, with Yandex DNS on its alternative port. Opened every blocked test site in live tests.</string>
    <string name="pd_tr_aggressive">Byte-by-byte fragmentation with out-of-order sending. Try it if others fail; slightly slower.</string>
    <string name="pd_tr_chunk">The original SpoofDPI-Türkiye setting: 5-byte TCP chunks. May not open some sites on some ISPs.</string>
    <string name="pd_tr_doh">Resolves names over encrypted HTTPS; the safest option against DNS tampering.</string>
